Mutation: internal/tui/tui.go's `createCWDGhostSuffix` was temporarily
replaced with `return ""` -- unconditionally disabling ghost rendering for
every field, not just the cwd field -- so the modal never draws a ghost
however it's driven.

To get the new step's OWN failure (rather than the pre-existing "text ...
has foreground token dimmed" assertion earlier in the same scenario tripping
first and skipping the rest, which is what happens when the whole scenario
is run against the mutant), the run captured below also temporarily dropped
that one earlier line from the scenario and ran only this scenario via its
tag; both the feature file and the tui.go mutation were reverted immediately
after, and the "revert confirmation" run above (all 6 scenarios, unmodified
feature file, unmodified tui.go) is the proof the revert is exact.

